{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cedq9DK1w4SqT6u9uH2Ji","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: needs_more_evidence\nCONSENSUS_BLOCKING: no\nRATIONALE: The core ruled proof is internally consistent at the receipt level: the producer now routes `ohlcData[1]` through `ohlcTimestampMs` (run-empire-v2.js:936-939), REST/liveness paths already pass milliseconds (1747-1748, 2905-2906), and StateManager's monotonic gate (core/StateManager.js:898-909) is unchanged. However, three obligations of the prompt are unmet: (1) nothing binds the attested artifact SHA-256s to commit a01582a0a95d7e42589dd3538961cf116a869d8f — the EVIDENCE.md cites a different predecessor SHA and a branch, so \"exact current-commit evidence\" is asserted, not proven; (2) `test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js` is a listed implementation file whose content was never supplied, so the test claim is uninspectable; (3) the mark update runs for ALL timeframes before the `tf === activeTf` gate — if the stream ever emits in-progress higher-timeframe candles carrying end-of-period (future) etimes, the monotonic gate would reject subsequent active-frame closes until the higher-tf bar completes. No receipt establishes closed-candle-only emission. These cap the verdict; none is a proven break.\nDISAGREEMENT: EVIDENCE.md's claim that \"repository-wide caller totality\" is \"closed by receipts\" is over-broad. The AST tape scans only the property name `updateLastPrice`. It does not scan for direct writes to `state.lastPrices` / `state.lastPriceTimes` Maps, which would bypass the monotonic gate entirely. Also, the \"trusted host probe\" output resides in a committed doc; the manifest attests the doc's bytes, not the execution — its execution provenance is testimony, not a host-attested trusted-path receipt.\nREQUIRED_RECHECK: (1) `git show a01582a0 --stat` plus per-file `git show a01582a0:run-empire-v2.js | sha256sum` compared against manifest artifact_sha256 566a2dac…; (2) supply `test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js:1-120` content at that commit; (3) receipt showing SessionRouter emission semantics — whether non-active-timeframe candles are closed-only or in-progress with future `etime` (the emitter feeding the handler at run-empire-v2.js:905); (4) AST scan for `lastPrices.set` / `lastPriceTimes.set` outside `updateLastPrice`.\nRECHECK_PROMPT: none (Mercury is unselected by explicit instruction; route the four rechecks above to the Kimi seat and the host operator, not Mercury).\nNEXT_CHECK: `git show a01582a0:run-empire-v2.js | sha256sum` — resolves the commit-binding uncertainty, which gates every other claim in this review.\n\nCANDIDATE SET: examined 16 of 19. Examined: all 16 manifest excerpts (run-empire-v2.js ×9 ranges; core/StateManager.js:898-909; foundation/ohlc-normalize.js:43-61; EVIDENCE.md ×3 ranges; REVIEW.md:16-37; ast-update-last-price.txt:3-32). Not examinable (content absent): CHANGELOG.md diff, `test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js` content, the commit object a01582a0 itself. M = 16 excerpts + 3 declared implementation touched files (CHANGELOG.md, run-empire-v2.js, test file), with run-empire-v2.js overlapping.\nAST EVIDENCE: tapes/host/ast-update-last-price.txt:3-32 — acorn strict + loose fallback, 635/635 tracked .js parsed, 13 `updateLastPrice` references enumerated, zero computed references, 4 loose-fallback files named. NAMED ABSENCE: no AST scan for direct `lastPrices` / `lastPriceTimes` map mutation (gate bypass), no AST arity check confirming every call site supplies the third `eventTimeMs` argument (omission silently injects `Date.now()`), and no model-side AST from Mercury (correctly not claimed).\nINHERITED (unfixed): run-empire-v2.js — `v: Number(raw?.v ?? raw?.volume ?? 0)` volume-zero trading-data default (:1627); `etime || latest.t` silent fallback (:1748, :2906); `?? (t + timeframeMs)` synthesized etime (:1616); `|| this.candleTimeframe` activeTf fallback (:934); CANDLE_NORMALIZED trace emits `etime` in seconds while LAST_PRICE_INFLUENCE emits `eventTime` in ms — mixed-unit trace representation. core/StateManager.js — `eventTimeMs = Date.now()` default parameter (:898) is a wall-clock silent default that would forever out-rank real event times if any caller omits the argument. foundation/ohlc-normalize.js — 1e12 seconds heuristic causing the acknowledged 1ms ms→s→ms truncation edge (:49). All unfixed; EVIDENCE.md:207-230 concedes the truncation edge as inherited.\nFOURTH SHAPE CLASSIFIER: classified 6 of 6. (1) `normalizeOhlcForProcessor` null-drop + handler warn (:910-913) — true boundary (external broker payload). (2) missing-symbol drop (:919-922) — true boundary. (3) StateManager monotonic reject (:905, pre-existing per EVIDENCE.md, not added in Part D) — true boundary tripwire. (4) `invalid liveness timeframe` throw (:2831) — producer-fixable (internal `getIntervalMs` config), loud, acceptable. (5) stale REST candle throw (:2846) — true boundary. (6) `etime || latest.t` fallback — silent default, not a receipted unreachability (etime is provably always finite post-normalize, making it dead code, but no unreachability receipt was filed).\nALLEGATIONS: A1 commit binding absent — MECHANICAL / RECEIPT(absence). A2 all-timeframe mark write + monotonic gate can starve active-frame marks if in-progress future-etime candles are emitted — SUBSTANTIVE / mechanism is RECEIPT, emission behavior unreceipted, so cannot raise found_break. A3 mixed-unit trace fields across adjacent trace events — MECHANICAL / RECEIPT. A4 test file content never supplied — MECHANICAL / RECEIPT(absence). A5 probe execution provenance is committed-doc TESTIMONY, not host-attested execution — MECHANICAL / TESTIMONY. A6 `Date.now()` default param + unverified call arity — MECHANICAL / RECEIPT. A7 caller-totality claim over-broad (no direct-map-write scan) — MECHANICAL / RECEIPT(absence).\nSUBSTANTIVE RESOLUTION: UNRESOLVED-FOR-TREY on A2. Mercury seat: unselected by explicit run instruction — no position exists and none may be attempted. Fable seat (this review): the mechanism is real at HEAD receipts — mark updates precede the `tf === activeTf` gate and the monotonic reject would suppress later active-frame closes behind any future-etime write; whether it fires depends on unproven emitter semantics. Kimi seat: pending downstream; Kimi must consume this exact output and rule on A2 with the emitter receipt if obtainable.\nWHAT I EXAMINED: all 16 host-attested excerpts and their manifest hashes; the AST tape methodology and full ref list; the probe command and output as written; EVIDENCE.md's producer-defect narrative and pre-change receipt; REVIEW.md's cap reasons and mechanical adjudication; prior-fixes ledger hook context.\nDID NOT EXAMINE: commit a01582a0 itself or any git object; `test/aggregate-source-backfill.test.js` content; CHANGELOG.md diff; the SessionRouter emitter feeding the :905 handler; StateManager readers of `lastPrices`; any Kimi output (none exists yet); any live runtime state.\nASSUMED: manifest SHA-256 attestation is honest for the supplied byte ranges; the pre-change receipt quoted in EVIDENCE.md accurately reflects predecessor 4878c01; the AST tape was produced on the trusted host as its header claims; `ohlcData[5]` is close price per the established 8-element OHLC array shape; no code edits were made in this read-only pass (none were)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28415,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28415},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-09-02T02:35:20.556Z","request_id":"req_011Cedq9AXavmM7Y5XsioAmN"}
